<gpx version="1.1" creator="Claude Bruce Trail planner" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Day 17 - Rattlesnake Point, Crawford Lake, Leech Porter</name></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.469506" lon="-79.913648"><name>P Start/finish parking</name><desc>Reservation system in effect. Paid: $12 per adult at gate, $10.50 online (+HST); no separate vehicle fee · book ahead</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.471920" lon="-79.950490"><name>P2 alternative parking</name><desc>Crawford Lake Conservation Area: Enter from Conservation Rd (formerly Steeles Ave), just east…. Paid: $12 per adult at gate, $10.50 online (+HST); no separate vehicle fee · book ahead. Joins the route near km 5.5 (210 m walk).</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.475257" lon="-79.934340"><name>J1</name><desc>J1: Continue straight onto the white-blazed main Bruce Trail, heading north-west. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off behind you.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.481305" lon="-79.940825"><name>J2</name><desc>J2: Turn left onto the blue-blazed Leech Porter Side Trail, heading north-west. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off on your right.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.477512" lon="-79.943475"><name>J3</name><desc>J3: Turn right onto the white-blazed main Bruce Trail, heading west. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off on your left.) The next 0.1 km follows an unopened road allowance (rough track, no traffic).</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.478134" lon="-79.947495"><name>J4</name><desc>J4: Continue straight onto the blue-blazed Crawford Lake Side Trail, heading south-west. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off on your left.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.468507" lon="-79.943385"><name>J5</name><desc>J5: Turnaround point. Turn around and retrace your steps.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
